{"id":37846,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/auxiliary-verbs-do-be-and-have/","parentId":542,"order":360,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"Auxiliary verbs: do, be and have","seo":{"title":"Auxiliary verbs: do, be and have - Test-English","description":"Learn how auxiliary verbs 'do', 'be' and 'have' form English tenses with this clear A2 grammar lesson with a rules, examples, and exercises.","image":"/media/uploads/Auxiliary-verbs-do-be-have_A2-grammar.webp"},"modified":"2026-02-24T17:53:42","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms of to complete the sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"1508\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct form for each gap below</h5> <div data-quiz=\"1509\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete each sentence with a verb from the box in the correct form.</h5> <p><span class=\"textBox\">arrive – break – drive – eat –&nbsp;forget – rain – repair – <del>send</del> – speak – understand – write</span><br> <br> <em>EXAMPLE: They have already <span class=\"textGap\">sent</span> the report.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"1510\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<p>In English, there are three main auxiliary verbs: <strong>do, be</strong> and <strong>have</strong>. They have negative and question forms. Other verbs need an auxiliary to make these forms.<br> <br> Modal verbs (<a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/can-cant/\"><strong>can</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/b1/can-could-be-able-to/\"><strong>could</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/may-and-might-whats-the-difference/\"><strong>may, might</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/have-to-dont-have-to-must-mustnt/\"><strong>must</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/should-shouldnt/\"><strong>should</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/will-and-shall/\"><strong>will</strong></a>, <strong>would</strong>) are also auxiliary verbs.<br> <br> <img src=\"/media/uploads/Auxiliary-verbs-Be-Do-Have_A2-grammar-chart.png\" alt=\"Grammar chart of auxiliary verbs do, be and have with forms, tenses and example sentences\" width=\"500\" height=\"589\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-44013\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Be</h2> <h4>Present and past continuous</h4> <p>We use <strong>be</strong> + –<strong>ing</strong> verb to form the present and past continuous.<br> <br> We use <strong>am/is/are</strong> + <strong>-ing</strong> to form the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-continuous/\">present continuous</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>is reading</strong></span> a book.</em></li> <li><em>They <span><strong>aren’t watching</strong></span> TV.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Are</strong></span> you <span><strong>studying</strong></span> for the test?</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>was/were</strong> + <strong>-ing</strong> to form the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/past-continuous-past-simple/\">past continuous</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>was cooking</strong></span> dinner at 8 o’clock.</em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>wasn’t sleeping</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Were</strong></span> they <span><strong>playing</strong></span> football?</em></li> </ul> <h4>Present and past simple passive</h4> <p>We use <strong>be</strong> + past participle to form the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/present-past-simple-passive/\">present and past simple passive</a>.</p> <p>We use <strong>am/is/are</strong> + past participle to form the present simple passive.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>English <span><strong>is spoken</strong></span> in many countries.</em></li> <li><em>The windows <span><strong>aren’t cleaned</strong></span> very often.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Is</strong></span> the homework <span><strong>finished</strong></span>?</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>was/were</strong> + past participle to form the past simple passive.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>The match <span><strong>was cancelled</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>The emails <span><strong>weren’t sent</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Were</strong></span> the tickets <span><strong>booked</strong></span> online?</em></li> </ul> <h2>Do</h2> <p>We use <strong>do/did</strong> + infinitive to make present and past simple negatives and questions.<br> <br> We use <strong>don’t/doesn’t</strong> + infinitive to make present simple negatives, and <strong>do/does</strong> + subject + infinitive to make <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple/\">present simple</a> questions.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>don’t like</strong></span> spicy food.</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>doesn’t work</strong></span> on Saturdays.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Do</strong></span> they <span><strong>live</strong></span> near here?</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>didn’t</strong> + infinitive to make past simple negatives, and <strong>did</strong> + subject + infinitive to make <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/past-simple-form-use/\">past simple</a> questions.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We <span><strong>didn’t go</strong></span> to the party.</em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>didn’t understand</strong></span> the question.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Did</strong></span> you <span><strong>finish</strong></span> the report?</em></li> </ul> <h2>Have</h2> <p>We use <strong>have</strong> + past participle (<strong>worked, played, seen, etc.</strong>) to form the present and past perfect.<br> <br> We use <strong>have/has</strong> + past participle to form the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/present-perfect/\">present perfect</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>has finished</strong></span> her homework.</em></li> <li><em>They <span><strong>haven’t visited</strong></span> the museum.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Have</strong></span> you <span><strong>seen</strong></span> this film?</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>had</strong> + past participle to form the <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/past-perfect/\">past perfect</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>had left</strong></span> before the meeting started.</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>hadn’t studied</strong></span> for the exam.</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Had</strong></span> they <span><strong>arrived</strong></span> when you called?</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":1508,"questions":[{"id":12913,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Why <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you working so late tonight?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["do","are","have"]}]},{"id":12914,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The emails <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> sent yesterday.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were","had","did"]}]},{"id":12915,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> she finished the report yet?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Has","Does","Is"]}]},{"id":12916,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> watching the match when I called.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["had","were","are"]}]},{"id":12917,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The windows <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> cleaned every week.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["have","are","do"]}]},{"id":12918,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> they invited to the wedding?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Were","Have","Did"]}]},{"id":12919,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> completed the course yet.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["isn't","didn't","hasn't"]}]},{"id":12920,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you doing at 9 o'clock last night?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were","did","had"]}]},{"id":12921,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The documents <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> signed by the manager.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["did","were","have"]}]},{"id":12922,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you ever visited Scotland?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Do","Have","Are"]}]}]},{"id":1509,"questions":[{"id":12923,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Tom ___ already left the office.</div>","choices":[{"id":24820,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> has</span>"},{"id":24821,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> is</span>"},{"id":24822,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> does</span>"},{"id":24823,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> was</span>"}]},{"id":12924,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The cake ___ made this morning.</div>","choices":[{"id":24824,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> did</span>"},{"id":24825,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> has</span>"},{"id":24826,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> was</span>"},{"id":24827,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> is</span>"}]},{"id":12925,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Let them play. They ___ doing anything wrong.</div>","choices":[{"id":24828,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>hadn't</span>"},{"id":24829,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> don't</span>"},{"id":24830,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> haven't</span>"},{"id":24831,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> aren't</span>"}]},{"id":12926,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We ___ waiting for you when you called.</div>","choices":[{"id":24832,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>are</span>"},{"id":24833,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have</span>"},{"id":24834,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> were</span>"},{"id":24835,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> did</span>"}]},{"id":12927,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The results ___ announced on the radio.</div>","choices":[{"id":24836,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> are</span>"},{"id":24837,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have</span>"},{"id":24838,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> did</span>"},{"id":24839,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> were</span>"}]},{"id":12928,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>___ she ever tried sushi?</div>","choices":[{"id":24840,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> Has</span>"},{"id":24841,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> Is</span>"},{"id":24842,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> Does</span>"},{"id":24843,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> Did</span>"}]},{"id":12929,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The lights ___ turned off last night.</div>","choices":[{"id":24844,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>have</span>"},{"id":24845,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> were</span>"},{"id":24846,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> are</span>"},{"id":24847,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> did</span>"}]},{"id":12930,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>At 8 p.m., I ___ still working.</div>","choices":[{"id":24848,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> have</span>"},{"id":24849,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>was</span>"},{"id":24850,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> am</span>"},{"id":24851,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> did</span>"}]},{"id":12931,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They ___ not completed the task yet.</div>","choices":[{"id":24852,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>were</span>"},{"id":24853,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> are</span>"},{"id":24854,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> did</span>"},{"id":24855,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> have</span>"}]},{"id":12932,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The museum ___ closed today.</div>","choices":[{"id":24856,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> isn't</span>"},{"id":24857,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> hasn't</span>"},{"id":24858,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> didn't</span>"},{"id":24859,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> wasn't</span>"}]}]},{"id":1510,"questions":[{"id":12933,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We can't play outside. It's <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> again.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12934,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Why are you so upset? Have you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> your keys?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12935,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The windows were <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> during the storm.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12936,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She was <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> home when the accident happened.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12937,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Mandarin is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> by over a billion people worldwide.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12938,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I don't <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> what you mean.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12939,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They have already <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the email.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12940,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>When we arrived, the guests were <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> dinner.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12941,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The computer is working again. It was <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> yesterday.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":12942,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Have you ever <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> late for an important meeting?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}